      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Every lever below was pulled on **2026-09-03**, so for about a week the rows will not separate\ncleanly — read the whole dashboard, not one panel. The outcome row is the only one that matters\non its own; the lever rows exist to say *which* change moved it.\n\n| Row | What we changed | Read it as |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lever 1 | Pruned CLAUDE.md and split the memory indexes two-level | a step down in **session baseline**, permanent |\n| Lever 2 | Added context-hygiene rules to the global instructions | **context added per turn** p90 falling toward p50 |\n| Lever 3 | Cut Bash/MCP/Task output caps to 12000 | **truncations** rising while **tool bytes per turn** falls |\n\n`spilled` is not a loss: the result went to a file and stays reachable. `chars`, `lines` and `kb`\ncut in place and that data is gone. `lines` and `overcap` byte counts are estimates.\n"
      },
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
